  "reason": "The records point in the right general direction but do not disclose the complete method. R1 provides the strongest basis: a near-DFT MTP for the closely related BCC NbMoTaW refractory alloy, showing that an MTP can represent chemically complex local environments. R16 separately identifies the uncertainty of EAM potentials at high temperature. R2 supplies related evidence that SRO contributes an energetic term in a similar refractory alloy, while R12, R13, R17, and R18 show that electronic or magnetic free-energy contributions and DOS behavior can alter phase stability. However, none of the records proposes a liquid-phase MTP for TaVCrW, replacing thermodynamic integration with MTP-to-DFT free-energy perturbation, or exploiting the low variance of MTP–DFT energy differences for rapid convergence. Thus an expert could infer the value of replacing high-temperature EAM sampling with an MTP and retaining electronic/SRO corrections, but FEP-based melting calculations and the integrated accelerated workflow would require a substantial new idea."
